  "summary": "The identified studies directly apply Bayesian hierarchical models, described as multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling, to the problem of customer churn (attrition). These models were evaluated across several datasets including ChurnBench, AgriSat-4, MetroFlow, and Atlas-ICU. Reported performance metrics vary by dataset and evaluation measure, with AUROC values of 0.65 on ChurnBench [V0209], MAE of 0.86 on AgriSat-4 [V0212], F1 of 0.72 on MetroFlow [V0210], and accuracy of 0.79 on Atlas-ICU [V0211]. While [V0009] mentions this modeling approach for customer attrition in passing, it focuses on septic deterioration and is included only as a peripheral reference.",
